From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rory Axton <roryaxton@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 04:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0979 redfin: scanout slots from the GPU pool at boot, no geometry
 ping-pong, back pressure by chain depth, retired SwapWait

r36a: CA's chain was two surfaces (2/3, after backboardd restarts 11/12,
28/29); slot 0 took one, the RAM slot for the other failed (XNU's RAM on
redfin is all above 4 GB, SRC0_ADDR is 32-bit), so every other frame was
non-slot and the pipes switched geometry on every frame. Now: slots 1-6
come from the GPU pool (unmanaged HLOS RAM below 4 GB, write-combined like
the carve-out), reserved in AppleCLCD::start (sweetscanslots, default 6);
one log line per panel-sized surface (slot or why not); direct only after
3 slot frames in a row; SwapEnd back pressure by CA's chain depth (N = 2:
until this frame is on screen); SwapWait until the swap is retired (a later
one on screen), at once on the normal path; latch = INTF1 frame counter
past the flush and VIG flush bits clear, or 2 frames; p mdp ca on an empty
slot shows the test pattern from that slot's memory.
---
